<h1>Week 34 Gross Profit Reconciliation Report</h1>
<p class="meta">
  <strong>Period:</strong> Tuesday 11 August 2026 – Monday 17 August 2026 (business week 34)<br>
  <strong>Prepared for:</strong> XXII Century / client review<br>
  <strong>Date:</strong> 14 September 2026<br>
  <strong>Subject:</strong> Comparison of client Gross Profit sheet vs system (OpenRoad-sourced) weekly report
</p>

<h2>1. Executive summary</h2>
<p>
We compared every driver card on the client workbook sheet <strong>W34 (2026)</strong>
against our live weekly Gross Profit calculation for the same Tuesday–Monday week.
</p>
<div class="box">
  <ul>
    <li><strong>77</strong> driver cards on the client sheet</li>
    <li><strong>68</strong> matched to drivers in our W34 active set</li>
    <li><strong>63 of 68 (93%)</strong> match on <strong>mileage</strong> within ±1 mile</li>
    <li><strong>48 of 68 (71%)</strong> match on <strong>total gross income</strong> within ±$1</li>
    <li><strong>48 of 68</strong> match on <strong>both</strong> miles and gross</li>
    <li><strong>5</strong> drivers have material mileage gaps</li>
    <li><strong>20</strong> drivers have gross gaps (often with miles already matching)</li>
    <li><strong>9</strong> sheet cards were not present in our W34 active report set</li>
  </ul>
</p>
</div>
<p>
<strong>Conclusion:</strong> This is not a random field-mapping error. Mileage alignment is strong.
Remaining differences are concentrated in (1) split-haul / multi-driver revenue allocation,
(2) a small set of drivers with different load coverage inside the week window, and
(3) secondary expense lines (pay, fuel, PrePass) that use different inputs.
</p>
<p>
The previously disputed example — <strong>Abdullahi Daud, unit 245</strong> — now
<strong>matches the client sheet on both mileage and total gross</strong>.
</p>

<h2>2. Scope and method</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Client source:</strong> workbook sheet <em>W34 (2026)</em> (77 GP cards; name, unit, mileage, total gross, expenses).</li>
  <li><strong>System source:</strong> live weekly summary from synced OpenRoad loads + driver_routes, assignments, compensations, fuel, Samsara MPG, and PrePass tolls.</li>
  <li><strong>Week rule:</strong> Tuesday → Monday (W34 = 2026-08-11 → 2026-08-17).</li>
  <li><strong>Match keys:</strong> truck unit where available, otherwise driver name.</li>
  <li><strong>Tolerance:</strong> ±1.0 mile for mileage; ±$1.00 for gross income.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Headline results</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Metric</th><th class="num">Count</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Client cards</td><td class="num">77</td><td>Full W34 card grid</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Matched to our roster / week set</td><td class="num">68</td><td>Unit or name match</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Mileage match (±1 mi)</td><td class="num"><span class="ok">63 / 68</span></td><td>93% of matched drivers</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Gross income match (±$1)</td><td class="num"><span class="warn">48 / 68</span></td><td>71% of matched drivers</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Both miles and gross match</td><td class="num"><span class="ok">48</span></td><td></td></tr>
  <tr><td>Mileage mismatches</td><td class="num"><span class="bad">5</span></td><td>See section 5</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Gross mismatches</td><td class="num"><span class="bad">20</span></td><td>See section 6</td></tr>
  <tr><td>On client sheet only (not in our W34 set)</td><td class="num">9</td><td>See section 7</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>4. Proof case — Abdullahi Daud (unit 245)</h2>
<p>
This driver was the primary example of a miles/gross gap earlier. After attributing
solo loads by delivery week and multi-driver helper segments from OpenRoad
<strong>driver_routes</strong>, the card matches the client sheet:
</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Field</th><th class="num">Client sheet</th><th class="num">Our system</th><th class="num">Difference</th><th>Result</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Mileage</td><td class="num">4,843.7</td><td class="num">4,843.65</td><td class="num">−0.05</td><td class="ok">MATCH</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Total gross income</td><td class="num">$12,007.60</td><td class="num">$12,007.60</td><td class="num">$0.00</td><td class="ok">MATCH</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Driver's pay</td><td class="num">$3,248.39</td><td class="num">$3,148.37</td><td class="num">−$100.02</td><td>Secondary (pay split / rates)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>PrePass</td><td class="num">$83.64</td><td class="num">$66.74</td><td class="num">−$16.90</td><td>Secondary (toll window / link)</td></tr>
</table>

